* These filters serve as signal conditioners. They have corner frequencies of 10kHz, \nso frequencies higher will be attenuated while our 500Hz signal passes through unaffected.\nThis means the amplitude and shape of Vvo and Vio will be kept the same before they're sampled.\nWe need these to keep unwanted high frequency noise from corrupting our measurement.
* Shunt Resistor is two 1 Ohm in parallel because our Pmax/I^2max was 0.565. We rounded down to 0.5 to keep worst case dissipation  under 200mW spec. \n \n56k/2.7k gives a 20.74 ratio, approximating the 20.78 ideal ratio.
